    <title>Storytellers</title>
    <desc>It’s that time again—when the boys from StruttinBuck load up and head out of Arkansas, bound for Fairfield, Texas and the FE Hill Ranch. Another year, another hunt, and another chapter in a tradition that’s grown into something far bigger than the hunt itself. This annual father-son trip is built on early mornings, shared stories, and moments that stick with you long after the season ends. It’s the memories made over the years that keep calling them back—and this year will be no different.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-5fd115b8b7ef8d002dcf1817" start="20261114091331 +0000" stop="20261114092631 +0000">
    <title>Storytellers</title>
    <desc>We join Blake Barnett alongside hunter Jimmy Reynolds as they take part in the 2nd Annual Pierce Dutton Memorial Hunt. This meaningful whitetail hunt is made possible by the great folks at Disabled Outdoorsmen. Jimmy settles in at the G2 Ranch in South Texas, where prime whitetail country and a shared passion for the outdoors set the stage for an unforgettable hunt.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-5fd115b8b7ef8d002dcf1817" start="20261114092631 +0000" stop="20261114093932 +0000">
    <title>Storytellers</title>
    <desc>We’re back with Double T Outfitters for this episode of Storytellers, filmed at the beautiful Las Lagunas Ranch in South Texas! - This hunt was one to remember as we spent time with the Price family, including Logan—our Show Your Skull Showdown winner from last season! From unforgettable hunts and incredible wildlife to evenings around hunting camp with amazing people, this trip was filled with memories that will last a lifetime. A huge thank you to Double T Outfitters for your incredible hospitality and for your continued support of TTHA. Partnerships like yours help make experiences like this possible. This episode is packed with great hunting, genuine friendships, and the stories that make the outdoors so special.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-5fd115b8b7ef8d002dcf1817" start="20261114093932 +0000" stop="20261114095302 +0000">
    <title>Storytellers</title>
    <desc>We’re kicking off a special weekend at Legends Ranch in Bitely, Michigan — bringing together two groups connected by a shared respect for the outdoors. Legends Ranch has always stood for - strong conservation values, and when you combine that with the work being done by the SCI Foundation and Sables, it sets the tone for something bigger than just a hunt. Sables members are deeply involved in shaping the future of hunting — reaching into - classrooms, working with young people, collaborating with wildlife professionals, and engaging leaders at both the state and national level. Their efforts are centered on helping others understand wildlife diversity, the principles behind the North American Model of Wildlife Conservation, and the role hunting plays in maintaining - balance in the wild. They’re also helping keep the tradition alive — showing that hunting still has a strong place in today’s culture and communities. With that kind of purpose behind it, this weekend is about more than time in the field — it’s about continuing something that matters.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-5fd115b8b7ef8d002dcf1817" start="20261114095302 +0000" stop="20261114100006 +0000">
    <title>TRP</title>
    <desc>On Today's How 2 Tuesday, we are testing the 5 most popular fishing knots that I know. When coming up with this episode I thought long and hard about which knots are popular and why, I hope you gain as much from this podcast as I did.  - Watch now to enhance your skills and improve your fishing game! Don't forget to subscribe for more practical fishing tips and tutorials. - Check out how this test compares to all the others I have done; get your FREE Knot Guide here! — - https://bit.ly/3UnAeIP - All Socials ⎯ - https://linktr.ee/TomRowlandPodcast - How2Tuesday is presented by Danco Pliers! - Danco Sports is an industry-leading manufacturer of pliers, knives, and accessories for anglers worldwide. Since our start in 2006, we have been committed to providing affordable, high-quality products and outstanding customer service to anglers and fishing leaders alike. Danco Pliers is located in Stuart, Florida, where we wear flip-flops to work year-round. - Check out Danco here — - https://bit.ly/tomrowlandpodcast2</desc>
  </programme>
  
